{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects","id":1558260,"title":"Radiations and their effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-12T06:43:47-08:00","id":1558260,"title":"Radiations and their effects","content":"The books i have are not very detailed about radiations. W20 say to treat them like fire damage, M20 say their damage apply every x minutes/seconds, nothing about radiations poisoning or soaking difficulty<br /> <br /> How do you deal with it? For environnemental i would say that damage are taken each turn for most violent radiations, scene for very dangerous, then x amount of minutes and hour for &quot;weaker&quot; one but i don't know what element to use for soaking difficulty. Type of ray? Intensity? Amount?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T10:49:00-08:00","id":1558261,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that radiation covers a huge spectrum of matter-energy interactions. The first step in what to do with radiation in a game is decide what kinds of radiation you want to model, and then how much you want to look at genre tropes vs more realistic metrics. Early WoD was very focused on a pop-culture heavy Cold War inspired &quot;green glow&quot; radiation concept, but later books backed off of that as that became less topical to most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T12:58:06-08:00","id":1558262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558261#post1558261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first step in what to do with radiation in a game is decide what kinds of radiation you want to model, and then how much you want to look at genre tropes vs more realistic metrics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to stay as realistic as possible for non supernatural case, and for radioactivity i'm talking to nuclear waste (used by fomori and bsd or simply in a nuclear incident sites if the story goes in that way). If the PC get in a place with radioactivity they will not feel anything until the dizziness begin, then the nose bleed, throw up etc... The violent irradiation is an invisible killer poisonning them, so when they begin to feel the firsts symptoms it's time for a soaking roll. Problem is frequency (turn - scene - minutes - hour(s), i need to do some research in order to set it according to the intensity)<br /> <br /> For supernatural attack i'm more open to some po culture representation like green ray/light emiting from the hand, shining in the eyes of a creature, and the supernatural attack would be treated in that case more like fire or the explosion charms from the spirit<br /> <br /> Then there's the poisoning effect. I dont think a Vampire would be hurt since they are living corpses but i've read that some specific sources like nuclear reactor produce ray that make their environnement and poor living being radioactive, so Vampire would not suffer from it but would become walking hazard without knowing (a fun but terrible joke)<br /> Werewolves would suffer from it while being exposed but aside from contamination like above they would not be suffering radiation poisoning thank to their healing factor, the book specificaly say that radioactive wound heal twice longer than regular aggr wound","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T14:11:39-08:00","id":1558263,"title":"","content":"&quot;Nuclear waste&quot; isn't really a thing in reality. The big concern are radioisotopes that form decay chains of ionizing radiation.<br /> <br /> So, first, ionizing radiation is the &quot;big deal&quot; because non-ionizing radiation is effectively harmless outsize of massive quantities. Ionizing radiation is dangerous because it knocks atomic particles out of position, which turns those atoms into ions, and thus makes them unstable and reactive; and in high enough doses is what leads to things like cancer and acute radiation poisoning.<br /> <br /> Decay chains are a problem because they increase the amount of radiation a given radioisotope can emit. Basically, a radioactive atom inevitably decays into a &quot;daughter&quot; atom as it sheds energy in the form of radiation. Most radioactive substances form stable daughter atoms after that initial shedding. The stuff that's really dangerous has a long chain of decaying from one radioactive daughter to another. So the more steps it takes to go from a radioactive parent to a stable multiple-granddaughter atom the more radiation is released; and if ionizing means it can do a lot of harm.<br /> <br /> More than 95% of &quot;waste&quot; from nuclear reactors are about as dangerous as getting an X-ray at the dentist's office. People that work around the waste need to monitor long term exposure, but generally it's safe because the radiation either isn't ionizing or doesn't have a decay chain associated with it. So it's a short small dose that goes away quickly. Above that there's the dangerous-but-not-immediately bad level of waste particles that can cause harm with exposure but can also be medically addressed if acted on quickly. Only after that do you have the tiny, tiny fraction of waste products that are in the really bad category.<br /> <br /> And those products aren't just mixed together when the waste is being processed; in fact quite the opposite. That's why situations like meltdowns are such a big deal: the safety protocols to contain the worst-of-the-worst waste particles get blown to bits and those get mixed in with all the minimal threat materials.<br /> <br /> Particle-Wave duality also makes things complicated to model. We treat radiation as a wave because most radiation acts as a wave, but the most dangerous &quot;rays&quot; are actually particles and are their most serious when they've &quot;calmed&quot; back to a particle behavior. An alpha or beta particle flying at you as a wave doesn't have the force to penetrate your skin or your clothing... that's why they have those emergency showers for people exposed to sudden high doses. But breathing in a lungful of beta particles? That can easily kill you because then they get into your body and sit there, shedding radioactive daughter chains, and so on. <br /> <br /> This doesn't really indicate much for putting soak into things for normal exposures. Obviously there is a physical component to it, but what ionizing radiation is going to do to you isn't something more endurance can change; only help you endure the process of trying to clean it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T15:13:07-08:00","id":1558264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558263#post1558263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This doesn't really indicate much for putting soak into things for normal exposures. Obviously there is a physical component to it, but what ionizing radiation is going to do to you isn't something more endurance can change; only help you endure the process of trying to clean it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the type of ray that could be used as a threat would be the ionizing one, and it seems if you convert it into damage it most likely would be unsoakable damage. Wich seems logical since it's not the flesh and bones that are damaged but their very cell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-12T17:21:25-08:00","id":1558273,"title":"","content":"Also, one of the reasons I brought up the particle-wave duality issue, is that alpha and beta particles (beta is the majority of nuclear radiation in reactors that builds up over time) - when acting as particles - don't just damage your cells. Once they get into your body they turn your atoms against you by ionizing them into radiation emitters as well through the decay chain. Even your non-living tissue like bones can get alpha (Polonium-210 poisoning works by flooding your system with alpha particles emitted from the polonium decay chain) or beta particles lodged in them and they would keep damaging your internal tissues. Some radioisotopes are very hard to detect (see polonium-210 again) because most radiation detectors focus on gamma rays (which are essentially photons and thus just really short but high intensity light that is easy to detect), so trying to purge them out of a body once they're in can be nearly impossible since you can't isolate where they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T02:09:31-08:00","id":1558278,"title":"","content":"So we talk in that case of contamination, Vampires would not be harmed because of their living corpse situation but would carry with them radioactivity and poison living being they encounter after their exposition. Human being, Mage and Werewolves would become their own source of &quot;poisoning&quot; since they would not be able to purge their contaminated cells unless using supernatural means (Gifts, spirits charms or true magic)<br /> <br /> So now we know that nuclear ionizing radiations, in terms of gameplay, should inflict non soakable damage and contaminate things and livings around their sources, poisoning them overtime even after leaving the area<br /> <br /> Now there's the frequency of damage application, wich would depend, when exposed, to how strong are the rays should they come from a source or their own contaminated body<br /> <br /> Aliens the Roleplaying game use a system that give player radiations point, giving how strong are the rays they can get them every 5/10 hours, every 5/10 minutes or every 5/10 seconds, each point are damage dice they roll each time they gain a new point. When they leave the area they lose a point every 5/10 hours but roll one die to know if instead of loosing a point it stay forever<br /> <br /> Warhammer 40k Wrath and Glory only say to roll each turn of exposition and suffer damage if you fail, the intenity affecting how much damage you take<br /> <br /> CoD use 4 environnemental level of lethality an inflict damage at a frequency depending on that level, hours for level 1 to 3 and turn at level 4 but does not give any detail on contamination and poisoning (but the environnemental level could become the character himself in case of contamination as an easy solution)<br /> <br /> It should be possible to make something inspired from one or the other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T03:31:16-08:00","id":1558279,"title":"","content":"Most of the WoD books imply that serious radiation sickness is Aggravated damage, which takes care of soak, the difficulty in treating/surviving for humans, and the higher tier magics needed for supernaturals to deal with it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd let vampires off that easily. Ionizing radiation chains are more serious against living tissue, but they can degrade most materials regardless. Dead cells are still going to get damaged and need to be repaired to full functioning. <br /> <br /> The problem with how much damage and over what interval is that the dose delivered is what matters and there's no simple way to calculate that. You keep saying &quot;rays&quot; but it's important to remember that radiation is really about particles unless you're next to a high output instant release of energy (like an atomic bomb or a nuclear meltdown). Think of something like pepper spray. A can of pepper spray could do nothing (you spray someone wearing a heavy coat on the back and they can just take off the coat and be fine), to extremely painful (spraying someone in the face or on open wounds) to deadly (spraying someone right in their mouth). You can absolutely do something like you suggest with different stages of intervals and the like, but most people have no idea what kind of exposure leads to what kind of dosage for what type of radioactive source. <br /> <br /> There's also an accumulation issue. If you're exposed to new radiation faster than you can deal with the old radiation in can compound more drastically than just the increase of damage levels would model well. Effectively this would mead both how much damage and how often you roll can both get worse depending on the type of exposure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T06:45:36-08:00","id":1558283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558279#post1558279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with how much damage and over what interval is that the dose delivered is what matters and there's no simple way to calculate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why but it make me think of the CoD environnemental threat level, the system is simple and is used in the game for radiations, storms and even tsunami, yet it's obviously more complex than that, being in a tsunami could mean simply drowning or being crushed by stuff water carry like cars. The system is designed to emulate the situation without dealing with most of details it would imply<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558279#post1558279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's also an accumulation issue. If you're exposed to new radiation faster than you can deal with the old radiation in can compound more drastically than just the increase of damage levels would model well. Effectively this would mead both how much damage and how often you roll can both get worse depending on the type of exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alien The Roleplaying Game and Fallout use an accumulation mechanic, both apply it differently though. Maybe there's a way to emulate very &quot;gamingly&quot; the exposition, accumulation and contamination from particles depending let's on how dangerous we would resume the situation instead of it's scientific detailed working","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T10:06:53-08:00","id":1558287,"title":"","content":"Trinity and Aberrant also deal with it, but just relate it as levels of bashing or lethal damage per turn, which is frankly unsatisfying.<br /> <br /> Accumulation in the WoD can only really be related back to &quot;you are already dead&quot; dosages on account of how frustratingly non-linear the ST system is. 1000 rads (1 gray or sievert) would, in that case, clock in at about seven levels of agg, with the caveat that exposure of this sort can still leave the victim alive for almost a day before they are no longer. A very rough equivalence could be something like Dose = (HL^2) * 20.5 rads (divide by 100 for Grays or sieverts), with any alpha radiation or other huge particles that get through counting as double to quadruple the number of rads. If you're calculating the other way, it'd be HL = sqrt (Dose/20.5), again with the dose in equivalent rads. You can potentially simulate the gradual lurching toward death by not applying wound penalties or being incapacitated immediately and instead just metering it out over the next roughly 18 hours.<br /> <br /> If you just want a simpler system, you can just rule that you suffer a health level every 100 rads equivalent of accumulation, and that the effects don't hit until (Stamina) hours later. Garou and most Fera get to roll to soak (repel, really) this damage, while vampires don't suffer damage but just keep accumulating rads and have to shed blood points in order to purge some of the longer-lasting particles or activated components of their body, or else they count as a source of radiation in the form of a wandering orphan source, which is probably a huge masquerade breach since it involves being able to move around mostly unimpaired when any human would have dropped dead. Some forms of radiation can count as being like fire to vampires instead, which brings the hazard of damage alongside accumulation of energy and dangerous materials (or activation of whatever the vampire has on or in them).<br /> <br /> Anyone else is affected by according to how resilient they are, except wraiths, who are already dead and made out of ectoplasm, which probably doesn't interact with radioactivity since it's the stuff of dead spirits... is what I'd say if WW wasn't arbitrarily weird about this, since ghosts of those slain by nuclear explosions seem to get twisted in some way for it and Yama Kings apparently cannot utilize their tainted energies, except for one who's experimenting with it (I think it was Ravana, who was trying to get India and Pakistan to commit MAD to harvest their dead. Stay classy, 90s WW!). The other Yama King who tried ended up comatose for his troubles (see: Dark Kingdom of Jade Adventures, specifically the one about snagging the relic nuke).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T10:33:26-08:00","id":1558288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558287#post1558287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you just want a simpler system, you can just rule that you suffer a health level every 100 rads equivalent of accumulation, and that the effects don't hit until (Stamina) hours later. Garou and most Fera get to roll to soak (repel, really) this damage, while vampires don't suffer damage but just keep accumulating rads and have to shed blood points in order to purge some of the longer-lasting particles or activated components of their body, or else they count as a source of radiation in the form of a wandering orphan source, which is probably a huge masquerade breach since it involves being able to move around mostly unimpaired when any human would have dropped dead. Some forms of radiation can count as being like fire to vampires instead, which brings the hazard of damage alongside accumulation of energy and dangerous materials (or activation of whatever the vampire has on or in them).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that a good way to at the same time keep it simple and accurate enough, just call that &quot;rads points&quot; and then make the pc roll to soak the cumulated rads and avoid damage. I assume that with more violent source of radiation (elephant foot or demon core) the rads would cumulate very quickly and the damage would occurs much sooner than hours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T12:55:06-08:00","id":1558291,"title":"","content":"To put some perspective of this, the fastest death attributed to the demon core experiments took 9 days, and the scientist in question got hit with an estimated 1,100 rad dose. The second fastest fatality from those experiments was 25 days after a 300 rad dose.<br /> <br /> The demon core dealt with a setup that generated mostly (~90%) neutron radiation, and the second most common product was gamma radiation (~10%). Both are short burst high intensity forms of ionizing radiation; the whole point was to work towards a functional neutron bomb because neutron radiation and gamma radiation disperse far more quickly than alpha or beta radiation. So a target hit with a neutron-primary device can be reclaimed faster.<br /> <br /> So it worked much more like &quot;rays.&quot; Louis Slotin, the one that died the fastest, was literally the one that cracked the containment sphere and got blasted in the stomach at point-blank, causing wide scale acute radiation poisoning to his gastrointestinal tract and widespread organ failure in the lower half of his torso.<br /> <br /> We don't really know what would have happened if his heart or brain would have taken the brunt of the burst; though we can presume he would have died faster simply because of the relative speed of death based on organ function.<br /> <br /> So something to consider might be to how vampire bases the amount of damage on surface area of exposure to fire or sunlight. Many of the victims of the demon core experiments survived for years or even decades (to the point where some are considered to have died from other causes) because they only got a glancing exposure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T14:52:58-08:00","id":1558295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558291#post1558291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So something to consider might be to how vampire bases the amount of damage on surface area of exposure to fire or sunlight. Many of the victims of the demon core experiments survived for years or even decades (to the point where some are considered to have died from other causes) because they only got a glancing exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire damage use the amount of body burning to set how many damage per turn you get, so a gaming setting using how much of the body's exposed and a roll (or st decision) to determine of some vital organs are affected could emulate this quite well imo<br /> <br /> I've found on this page a table with 6 different exposition in Gray, it give the amount and the time unit where it affect the victim. I think it can be used to forge a gaming system with the Intensity and frequency of damage<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syndrome_d%27irradiation_aigu%C3%AB\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Radioactive.svg/1280px-Radioactive.svg.png?utm_source=fr.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syndrome_d%27irradiation_aigu%C3%AB\" target=\"_blank\"> Syndrome d'irradiation aigu&euml; &mdash; Wikip&eacute;dia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syndrome_d%27irradiation_aigu%C3%AB\" target=\"_blank\"> https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syndrome_d%27irradiation_aigu%C3%AB </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 02-13-2026, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-22T06:35:52-07:00","id":1558967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558279#post1558279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'd let vampires off that easily. Ionizing radiation chains are more serious against living tissue, but they can degrade most materials regardless. Dead cells are still going to get damaged and need to be repaired to full functioning.</div> </div> </div> </div>A while back the question came up whether the daily reset which returns vampires to the state of Embrace would also cover ionized tissue. I'm still not sure how I would handle this. Dealing with the physical damage is one thing, becoming a walking orphan source is an entirely different can of problems.<br /> <br /> I can see the argument that ionized particles could count as 'alteration', but having the stasis effect cancel out nuclear decay feels like a bit much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-22T12:23:23-07:00","id":1558968,"title":"","content":"Consider the books are consistent that daily &quot;reset&quot; doesn't cover damage or the physical manifestations of it, I don't really see the case if there's enough radiation to be thinking about marking off damage. If a vampire's hand gets cut off, it stays cut off until enough vitae goes to regrowing it. It doesn't come back non-functional the next day or something like that. A vampire can be stuck under rubble indefinitely because even if they heal the crush damage they can be too weak to escape and etc. The rocks don't start breaking because the vampire's body is constantly resetting and crushing and the repeat motion breaks up the rubble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-23T04:38:41-07:00","id":1558971,"title":"","content":"Ah, the question was less about healing damage and more about induced radioactivity by a high gamma or neutron source - like, would the vampire click a dosimeter after they healed the damage, or would that be gone the next day?<br /> <br /> Or the other way around, if you would radiocarbon date an ancient, would the isotopes indicate old or recent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-23T10:27:32-07:00","id":1558976,"title":"","content":"The problem is magic.<br /> <br /> What the daysleep reset can and can't undo isn't some in-universe undead-biology rule. It's a magic rule with narrative purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-23T11:22:05-07:00","id":1558977,"title":"","content":"Probably a lot of noise in the signal indicating everyone that the vampire has drained. If applied rigorously, this could, in fact, be the equivalent of &quot;how many breads you've eaten&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T06:57:27-07:00","id":1558990,"title":"","content":"Vampires can be carriers for some blood bourn diseases, so the reset doesn't handle everything. Beyond that, I think it is more a question of what is appropriate to the Chronicle than any specific game rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-24T11:33:47-07:00","id":1558995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558977#post1558977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably a lot of noise in the signal indicating everyone that the vampire has drained. If applied rigorously, this could, in fact, be the equivalent of &quot;how many breads you've eaten&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Netchurchian kind of venture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558990#post1558990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can be carriers for some blood bourn diseases, so the reset doesn't handle everything. Beyond that, I think it is more a question of what is appropriate to the Chronicle than any specific game rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, something for Purity of Flesh then. On the other hand, &quot;Radioactive&quot; might be an interesting spin on the Disease Carrier flaw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1558976#post1558976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, but I tend to try and use a system's magic rules to alleviate handwaves if I can. If nothing else, it's fun to hypothesize at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T08:04:50-07:00","id":1562084,"title":"","content":"I think this is going more complex than it needs.<br /> <br /> Setting aside all the things we thought to know about radiation but didn't (a lot of long term predictions failed in favor of the victims), first order of business should be: what kind of result we need to model to begin with?<br /> <br /> At the end in the day, radiation effects in the body boil down to five things:<br /> <br /> 1. Acute Radiation Sickness. Ionizing damage, that destroy the chemical properties of molecules, plays a number on your biochemistry at a massive scale, primarily by unmaking DNA. At this scale cancer is not a big concern.<br /> <br /> 2. Cancer rates. This is the least understood effect in prediction models. It relies on small, cumulative damage over a long time, as bigger damage is more likely to destroy DNA than render it cancerous.<br /> <br /> 3. Heat. This is rare, but straightforward. Most sources we understand as &quot;radiation&quot; won't get this hot, neither will you as a secondary source after contamination. When this happens its exactly what says in the tin.<br /> <br /> 4. Contamination. Alpha particles, Beta particles, and sometimes good old dust. This is a big problem, but also straightforward. Surface contamination can be washed, internal depends on contaminated tissue. Sometimes you have a cascading of ionization, others your kidneys can work through it.<br /> <br /> 5. Regular poisoning. Radioactive materials are also materials. They have their own chemical properties. Many will poison you regardless, like Plutonium compromising bone or Uranium causing fibrosis in the lungs. Some materials have no toxicity, and most can be flushed by the body with varying ease if you survive, which isn't necessarily hard. Polonium is virtually always lethal, while uranium is actually a common contaminant that requires abnormal doses to be a big problem.<br /> <br /> The thing is: cancer and most poisoning are long term effects. We're talking years, decades after exposure, and even then very inconsistent results. Do we need to track this? Do we track all the other things that affect cancer rates, can cause long term poisoning or bioaccumulate? Radiation is far from unique in this area.<br /> <br /> Heat is so specific to certain situations it isn't worth a rule, either. Some sources are hot is all we need to know.<br /> <br /> Seriously I think we only need to model Acute Radiation Sickness and Contamination, even then the last one as a secondary rule for plots where tracking sources is relevant.<br /> <br /> My opinion is that this is better handled as delayed damage. You roll for Soak upon exposure if you can Soak Agg, but the actual damage comes hours or days later. Base the effect in the exposure level (there's a table somewhere I can look for later) and call it a day.<br /> <br /> How to define exposure level? Make it up. We have no general protocols because it depends on a lot of fine details. Not just &quot;amount&quot;, but type of radiation, intensity, the material in question, background radiation at the area, material presentation, intake/exposure method...<br /> <br /> Your best bet is detecting Sieverts, but there's no such a thing as ambient sieverts or source sieverts/minute. This unit refers to the amount of energy absorbed by tissue, so it's detected only after the fact. So... Yeah. Make it up for each particular case, only rule of thumb is that for most cases the bigger increase happens if a source is inhaled or ingested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-25T23:14:13-07:00","id":1562172,"title":"","content":"While not the ultimate source of info on it, and with a few errors, you can do worse than look at Wikipedia for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acute_radiation_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\">Acute</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acute_radiation_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\">Radiation</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acute_radiation_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\">Syndrome</a>. The table there is good enough for a game and there are some useful explanations.<br /> <br /> The gist of it is: acute exposure (which means a lot) causes three stages of problems. The first stage has the symptoms derived from direct damage to chemical species. This ranges from sudden burn-like lesions to diarrhea, fever and others that could have been caused by several other things.<br /> <br /> After some hours or a few days, you get better. In fact, you may get really well. Some patients said those days were their healthier in years for in their whole lives. This is called the Latent Period and can last more than a month, and it is bittersweet, because this is the worse sign possible.<br /> <br /> Reality behind the Latent Period: DNA was destroyed in scale. For most cells this means little in the short run, while microbes are dead. Your body cleansed the worse of direct damage. But with extremely damaged DNA your cells can't replicate. Some systems, like Blood and Immunity, require constant replication, but their initial shut down actually makes you feel better.<br /> <br /> You're not good. You're collapsing, and the alarm systems are the first to go under. You're already doomed at this point unless being taken care. Sometimes patients in this stage are left to go home so they can enjoy their last days.<br /> <br /> Lastly the symptoms of the second phase come crashing fast. This is catastrophic collapse. At this stage you're dead under certain definitions already and recovery is impossible, either you'll survive hell and keep the scars or, more likely, not.<br /> <br /> Successful treatment usually stabilize you in first stage. If it evolves to Latent your chances are slim, but still there if treatment continues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T08:16:40-07:00","id":1562261,"title":"","content":"It's not just that your cells can't replicate, they also can't produce the proteins they need to function. Even the slowly replicating cells will cease to function properly as they run out of the proteins they use and produce and can no longer make more. <br /> <br /> Incidentally, this is quite similar to what happens with certain kinds of mushroom poisoning, and for similar reasons. The mushroom toxins in deathcaps don't damage the DNA directly but they do inhibit enzymes vital to transcription. Cells can no longer synthesize proteins. There's even the same three phase progression: acute symptoms, a walking ghost latency period, and rapid collapse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T11:32:05-07:00","id":1562267,"title":"","content":"I didn't cite the protein transcription because it's less universal. Breaking the replication process is easier than breaking every RNA transcription at once. That's possibly the cause of the latency period: the symptoms of protein failure end, the symptoms of replication failure still didn't start.<br /> <br /> But similar result, nonetheless. The walking ghost period is the most iconic sign of ARS or Deathcap poisoning, so this is the single thing that really need special rules for radiation. All other possible maladies are either covered by regular rules or happen in a scale that doesn't make sense to track.<br /> <br /> For supernaturals, I think Vampires should be immune to ARS: there's no metabolism or transcription to be messed with. At the point it is seriously causing structural damage it's also already burning.<br /> <br /> Werewolves? I'm inclined to let them pass, too. Their regeneration is a spiritual power. If they're virtually immune to diseases, poisons and recover from any wound, DNA damage shouldn't be too hard. But I'd understand it not being the case if the ST wants to explore radiation as having a spiritual side to the damage.<br /> <br /> Demons should be equally immune while they have remaining Faith points, per the same reasons, and with the same &quot;unless radiation is magic&quot; caveat.<br /> <br /> Others receive damage like normal people, so nothing changes for them.<br /> <br /> Wraiths would demand careful consideration to the Rule of Ouch, but probably it isn't sufficiently overt to demand this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T12:27:22-07:00","id":1562268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1562267#post1562267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraiths would demand careful consideration to the Rule of Ouch, but probably it isn't sufficiently overt to demand this.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a strict read wraith's go Incorporeal in collisions with skinlands objects and the Rule of Ouch is stated in terms of impacts, so as written I'm not sure even the hottest fire would make Wraiths go Incorporeal. However, there is one line at the end of the Rule of Excuse Me sidebar that indicates that the reminder of a wraith's ephemeral state is what makes him go Incorporeal. I could see that same element in play if the wraith were in a bonfire.<br /> <br /> With nothing to physically impact and nothing obvious to remind a wraith of his state, I don't think radiation would do anything at all. Even if it did, I don't think it would do anything besides the single point of bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Shadowlands radiation, if such a thing is in play, could do a lot more but I don't think it would cause any kind of ghostly ARS because wraiths simply aren't made that way. Although given the causes of the 5th and 6th Great Maelstroms (especially the 6th) it is possible that significant radiation could contribute to a lesser maelstrom forming.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T13:18:40-07:00","id":1562272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558260-radiations-and-their-effects?p=1562268#post1562268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a strict read wraith's go Incorporeal in collisions with skinlands objects and the Rule of Ouch is stated in terms of impacts, so as written I'm not sure even the hottest fire would make Wraiths go Incorporeal. However, there is one line at the end of the Rule of Excuse Me sidebar that indicates that the reminder of a wraith's ephemeral state is what makes him go Incorporeal. I could see that same element in play if the wraith were in a bonfire.<br /> <br /> With nothing to physically impact and nothing obvious to remind a wraith of his state, I don't think radiation would do anything at all. Even if it did, I don't think it would do anything besides the single point of bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Shadowlands radiation, if such a thing is in play, could do a lot more but I don't think it would cause any kind of ghostly ARS because wraiths simply aren't made that way. Although given the causes of the 5th and 6th Great Maelstroms (especially the 6th) it is possible that significant radiation could contribute to a lesser maelstrom forming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> I think an explosion or some really overt event of radiation damaging things could trigger the effect. But unless &quot;Radiation is Magic&quot; is in play, that won't go beyond the regular Ouch.<br /> <br /> On the Maelstroms, radiation was not the only thing, and was of very specific types. I'd refrain from causing a Maelstrom out of radiation alone. Though anything that releases so much energy is likely to not be radiation alone anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}